  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$H=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-3 & 8 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the $3$rd row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(H) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-3 & 8 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-3 & 8 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & \\,\\,\\,-3 & 8 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $1$st row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-6-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
